  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-78473",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=f(-x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $y$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(2,-4)$ lies $2$ units to the *right* from the $y$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected $2$ units to the *left* from the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224557/assets/456a145820b2a36693df572b49064332a18a2e79c35f2a0e3240b9995660c9a5.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point $(-2,-4)$ must lie on the graph of $y=f(-x).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
